                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "datasource-influxdb"
                      },
                      "group": "influxdb",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "alias": "$tag_battery_id / $tag_cell_id",
                        "query": "SELECT mean(\"voltage_delta\") * 1000\nFROM \"pylontech/cell\"\nWHERE $timeFilter\nGROUP BY time($__interval), \"battery_id\", \"cell_id\" fill(previous)",
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "resultFormat": "time_series"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Each cell's voltage minus the mean of its own battery (pylontech/cell voltage_delta, in mV). Green is within ±5 mV of the module. Blue shades are cells below their module, i.e. holding less charge: the ones that reach the low knee first and lag at the top of charge. Yellow to red shades are cells above their module: the ones that hit the high-voltage limit first. Judge at rest (current ≈ 0) after an hour of relaxation; under load or during absorption a ±30 mV spread is normal.",
          "id": 8,
          "links": [],
          "title": "Pylontech Cell Voltage Delta to Battery",
